This looks like spring 2021. Unemployment is 6.0%, which matches March 2021, and the 10-year yield is 1.65%, consistent with end of March 2021 (about 1.74% at month-end, or 1.65% as a monthly average). Headline CPI at 2.64% fits March 2021 (2.6%), and core CPI at 1.65% also matches (1.6%). The 3-month average payroll gain of 539k is consistent with Jan–Mar 2021, and the 12-month equity return of 46% fits March 2021 (from the March 2020 low).

Industrial production YoY of +1.02% is consistent with March 2021. The VIX of 17.61 is low for that month, but it is plausible given the 3-month change of -15.48 (a 3-month-earlier level of about 33 seems too high for December 2020, but it may reflect a different measure). Overall, March 2021 is the best fit.

